  "title": "The Record-Groove Express",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "miniature adventure",
  "premise": "A toy traveler must reach a label at the center of a slowly turning oversized record, but walking straight keeps carrying them sideways. They ride a fictional groove-following sled inward, step onto the stationary display spindle platform, and discover the parcel was a tiny dance invitation.",
  "hook": "The road goes around. The address is in the middle.",
  "visible_action": "Record turns slowly; footsteps arc; a sled follows an inward spiral; traveler dismounts at a fixed center platform.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A route can follow the landscape instead of fighting it.",
  "gate": "Use an invented oversized display model, not a real turntable; do not claim actual record grooves form a practical ride.",
